# The McFly backend this repo's displays connect to by default: mcfly.bot's
# Supabase project. Both values are public (the URL and the anon key ship in
# every browser that opens the console); the database's row-level security is
# what protects the data. install-pi.sh copies them into
# /etc/mcfly/display.env when that file has no backend of its own yet, so a
# fresh install opens straight on the pairing code. To use another project,
# run ./display/deploy/connect-backend.sh afterwards.
